<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy | HS GPA Calc" description="HS GPA Calc privacy policy: your grades stay in your browser. We don't collect, sell or share the data you enter into the calculator." path="/privacy-policy/" heading="Privacy Policy" updated="October 15, 2026">
  <p>HS GPA Calc ("we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what happens to information when you use hsgpacalc.com.</p>
  <h2>Information you enter</h2>
  <p>The class names, grades, credits and settings you enter into the calculator are stored only in your browser using localStorage. They are not sent to our servers, and we cannot see them. Clearing your browser data or using the Reset button removes them.</p>
  <h2>Share links and exports</h2>
  <p>If you use Copy Link, your entries are encoded inside the link itself. Anyone who has the link can see those entries, so share it only with people you trust. CSV exports are created on your device.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to understand how many people visit the site and which pages they use. Google Analytics may set cookies and collect information such as your approximate location, device and browser type, and pages viewed. It does not receive the grades or class details you enter into the calculator. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> or by blocking cookies in your browser.</p>
  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, and analytics are provided by Google Analytics. Google may receive your IP address and browser information when the page loads, according to Google's own policies.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The calculator is designed for students, and it doesn't ask for any personal information such as names, emails or ages.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
